// Lesson 8.2 — Boss Prototype I: Arena, Body & Health
// Level 3 (Outline Only): build a rough playable boss arena & body quickly using reused
// parts (`EnemyController`, `Platform`, `TurretController`, `StatManager`, Cave tilemaps)
// so something can be fought and tested immediately — greybox first, art polish later.
import Lesson from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';
import { renderAskBanner } from '../../lib/walkthrough';
import { renderDecompose } from '../../lib/decompose';

const DECOMPOSE = {
  big: 'Prototype the boss room, body, and health state quickly so the fight is playable today.',
  parts: [
    {
      name: 'Build the greybox arena with existing cave tiles, platforms, and tags',
      doc: '7.1 / 6.3 (tilemap colliders tagged `Ground`, moving `Platform` lifts, `Ladder` triggers)',
      href: '6.3.html',
    },
    {
      name: 'Assemble the boss body, tag it Enemy, and wire ChangeHealth() + Phase threshold',
      doc: '4.1 / 4.6 (`EnemyController.health`, `ChangeHealth()`, and `Enemy` tag for melee checks)',
      href: '4.1.html',
    },
  ],
  why:
    'Prototyping means getting a rough version running in 20 minutes rather than spending two days tweaking sprites on an unplayable boss. Reusing `Enemy` tags and `EnemyController` (or a small custom boss script reusing `ChangeHealth()`) lets you test room scale, jump height, and attack reach right away.',
  turns: [
    'Before decorating anything, what is the single fastest test you can run in Play mode today to verify your arena spacing works with `gravityScale` and `jumpForce`?',
    'Look at `PlayerController.OnTriggerEnter2D()`: why does tagging your boss (or its weak spots) `"Enemy"` make `currentEnemy` and `KeyCode.E` melee work automatically?',
  ],
};

const body = `
${renderAskBanner('how do I prototype a boss using parts I already built?', 3)}

<p class="lead">
    <strong>Day 1 of building on your own: Prototype fast.</strong> Put an ugly, playable version of
    your boss fight on screen today using tilemaps, existing sprites, moving <code>Platform</code> lifts,
    and <code>EnemyController</code> (or a fresh <code>BossController</code> carrying health and a
    phase check). Real feedback only starts once you can jump around the room and hit something.
</p>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
${renderDecompose('8.2', DECOMPOSE, 3)}

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">In the Editor: Greybox Arena &amp; Boss Body (~30 min)</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~30 min</span>
    </div>

    <ol>
        <li>Create your boss room (either at the end of <code>Platformer.unity</code> behind a door/checkpoint, or as its own scene added to <code>File → Build Profiles</code> with a <code>SceneSwitch</code> entrance).</li>
        <li>Paint solid floor/wall geometry tagged <code>Ground</code>, place any <code>Platform</code> lifts or <code>Ladder</code> triggers from your <a href="8.1.html">8.1</a> sketch, and drop a backup <code>StatManager</code> (or enter from <code>Start (index 0)</code>).</li>
        <li>Create the <code>Boss</code> GameObject (or compose it from child parts — armored shell + glowing core / mounted <code>Turret</code> children), add a solid collider plus a slightly larger trigger collider tagged <code>Enemy</code>, and give it high starting health (e.g. <code>10</code>–<code>15</code>).</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic: Prototyping Scale &amp; Ownership</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>In a multi-part boss (e.g., giant sprite + glowing weak point), which child should carry the <code>"Enemy"</code> trigger tag — the whole body or only the exposed weak point? What changes for the player?</li>
            <li>How does the player know from watching the screen that the boss actually lost health without staring at Unity's Inspector? Name two cheap visual signals (color flash, scale pulse, Phase 2 sprite/turret waking up).</li>
            <li>If the player spawns inside the boss arena on retry after <code>StatManager.Die()</code>, where should the player transform start so they never take unavoidable frame-1 contact damage?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">In the Code: Health, Damage &amp; Phase State (~25 min)</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~25 min</span>
    </div>

    <p>
        Whether you reuse <code>EnemyController</code> directly or duplicate it into a dedicated
        <code>BossController.cs</code> script, keep the clean contract your player already speaks:
    </p>

    <table>
        <tr><th>Part</th><th>How It Works</th><th>Reused Pattern</th></tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>public int health</code> / <code>maxHealth</code></td>
            <td>Exposed/initialized on the boss; higher than a hallway grunt so the fight spans phases.</td>
            <td><code>EnemyController</code> &amp; <code>StatManager</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>public void ChangeHealth(int amount)</code></td>
            <td>Adds negative <code>amount</code> on hit, flashes sprite or logs damage, switches Phase 2 below half health, calls <code>Die()</code> at <code>&lt;= 0</code>.</td>
            <td><code>EnemyController.ChangeHealth()</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>bool phaseTwo = false;</code></td>
            <td>Flipped once when <code>health &lt;= maxHealth / 2</code> to speed up movement, unlock extra turrets, or activate platforms.</td>
            <td>State flag like <code>isPlatformer</code> / <code>isOn</code></td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic: Reusing vs. Extending</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Why is copying <code>EnemyController.cs</code> into <code>BossController.cs</code> safer than rewriting hallway enemies — what happens to every ordinary cave enemy if you edit <code>EnemyController</code> directly to spawn phase-2 turrets?</li>
            <li>Check your damage math: <code>PlayerController</code> deals <code>-1</code> per <code>KeyCode.E</code> melee swing on a <code>0.5f</code> cooldown. With your chosen boss <code>health</code>, how many clean hits does it take to defeat the boss?</li>
            <li>If <code>phaseTwo</code> triggers inside <code>ChangeHealth()</code>, why do we guard it with <code>if (!phaseTwo &amp;&amp; health &lt;= maxHealth / 2)</code> instead of letting phase-transition logic run every time the boss gets hit below half HP?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic: Self-Check Before Attack Wiring</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Walk your prototype arena right now in Play mode (even before the boss attacks back): can your player reach every high platform with single or double jump, and never get trapped in a corner?</li>
            <li>Does pressing <code>J</code> near walls accidentally refill jumps, or is only walkable floor tagged <code>Ground</code>?</li>
            <li>Can you defeat your greybox boss? Write down how long the bare fight takes in seconds — that baseline guides tomorrow's tuning.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="checklist">
    <h3>Checkpoint — before moving on, you must be able to:</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Build a playable greybox arena reusing cave tilemaps, <code>Platform</code> lifts, and ladders</li>
        <li>Place a tagged boss body with working health (<code>ChangeHealth()</code>) and a Phase 2 threshold</li>
        <li>Verify arena jump spacing and sightlines in Play mode before adding heavy attack logic</li>
        <li>Commit and push</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <p>Need a deeper explanation? These pages cover the same concepts:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-08/index.html">Unit 8: Boss Fight</a> — prototyping &amp; reuse notes</li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-04/enemy-state-machines.html">Enemy State Machines</a> — <code>EnemyController</code> walkthrough</li>
        <li><a href="../docs/ask.html">How do I&hellip;? index</a> — find this lesson again by the question you were asking</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Next: <a href="8.3.html">8.3 — Boss Prototype II: Player Attacks &amp; Hitbox</a> — make melee and fireballs register cleanly on the boss.</p>
</div>`;
---
<Lesson id="8.2" title="8.2 Boss Prototype I: Arena, Body &amp; Health — AP CS Principles" root=".." css="../style.css">
  <Fragment set:html={body} />
</Lesson>
